>> title: Hand-Folded Pork and Cabbage Dumplings
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hour 20 minutes
>> tags: centerpiece, watchme, dumplings, folding, prep-heavy

Toss @napa cabbage{2%cups} with @kosher salt{1%tsp} in a #bowl{} and rest for ~{10%minutes}.

Squeeze cabbage dry in a #clean towel{}.

Mix cabbage with @ground pork{12%oz}, @scallions{3}, @ginger{1%tbsp}, @soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @sesame oil{2%tsp}, and @white pepper{1/4%tsp}.

-- watch: Filling mound is centered and small enough to leave a clean wrapper border.
Place @dumpling wrapper{1} on a #cutting board{} and add @filling{1%tsp}.

Moisten the wrapper edge with @water{} using a #finger{}.

-- watch: Pleats are even, edge is fully sealed, and filling does not squeeze out.
Fold wrapper in half and pleat one side against the other to seal.

Repeat with remaining @dumpling wrappers{36} and filling.

Heat @neutral oil{1%tbsp} in a #non-stick skillet{} and arrange dumplings flat-side down.

-- watch: Dumpling bottoms are golden brown before water is added.
Cook uncovered for ~{3%minutes}.

Add @water{1/3%cup}, cover, and steam for ~{7%minutes}.

Uncover and cook until water evaporates and bottoms re-crisp, about ~{2%minutes}.

Serve with @dumpling dipping sauce{}.
